course: dictionary
lesson: 12395
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Cupping is one of them. The words around it give you clues about which meaning the writer means. «She was cupping water in her hands and drinking from the stream.» Here cupping is an action: she is holding her hands in a curved shape like a cup.
explain: «The doctor talked about cupping, a treatment with cups placed on the skin.» Here cupping is a name for a treatment. Ask yourself: is the word about a person doing something, or about a thing or a treatment?
explain: «At the coffee shop, the expert spent an hour cupping the beans to test their flavour.» This is a third meaning: a careful tasting of coffee by smelling and slurping it. The clues are coffee and flavour. If your first meaning does not fit, try another one and check the sentence again.
fact: Cupping means holding your hands in a curved shape like a cup.
fact: «Cupping your ear» means holding your hand behind your ear to hear better.
fact: Cupping therapy is an old treatment in which cups are placed on the skin and the air in them is reduced, so the skin is sucked up and leaves round marks.
fact: Some people believe cupping therapy helps aches, but there is little good scientific evidence that it works.
fact: In the coffee and tea trade, cupping is a careful tasting: people smell and slurp the drink to judge its quality.
exercise: «She was cupping water in her hands to drink.» What does cupping mean here? | A treatment with glass cups on the skin | Pouring water onto the ground | Tasting coffee with a loud slurp | *Holding your hands in a curved shape like a cup
exercise: «The doctor explained cupping therapy, which leaves round marks on the skin.» What is cupping in this sentence? | A way of holding your hands together to pray | A loud shout for help | Tasting tea to judge it | *An old treatment in which cups are placed on the skin
exercise: «The expert spent the morning cupping coffee to judge its quality.» Which meaning fits best? | *A careful tasting of coffee by smelling and slurping it | A medicine taken with a glass of water | Drawing a cup on a page | Holding your hands in a curved shape
test: Ben stood still, cupping his ear to hear the birds. What was Ben doing? | *Holding a hand behind his ear to hear better | Covering both ears to block out the noise | Tasting the birdsong like coffee | Shouting at the birds
test: Some people say cupping therapy helps aches. Why might a careful reader ask, «What is the evidence?» | It is a kind of coffee | It means holding your hands like a cup | The marks always go away at once | *Because some people believe it helps, but there is little good scientific evidence
exam: «Cupping the baby bird gently, Mia carried it back to its nest.» What does cupping mean here? | Pushing it hard away | Singing a song to it | Tasting its feathers | *Holding it gently in hands curved like a cup
